    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for today centers heavily on **Jackson Merrill**, who stands as our only elite-tier play with a score of 66.54. Positioned in the #2 hole against May (3.99 xERA), **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a massive +13% platoon efficiency boost, cementing his status as the cornerstone of our lineup. While **Drake Baldwin** lands at 50.51, his value is propped up largely by his leadoff spot, though he faces a difficult test against Yamamoto; the +10% order bonus is essentially keeping him afloat against a high-caliber arm. \n\nThe outfield configuration remains a point of concern as we face the formidable Chris Sale. **Kyle Tucker** (47.59) and **Andy Pages** (43.88) are both hovering near the margin of the starting threshold, as their raw production is stifled by a significant -19% penalty due to the elite xERA of our opponent. We are effectively playing for efficiency here; **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s score is dampened by an suboptimal #8 slotting, but we are keeping him active in hopes that he can leverage his plate discipline to scrape out value in a low-scoring environment. We considered rotating in reserve infielders like **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** or **Brayan Rocchio** to chase potential stolen base volume, but their projected plate appearances against top-tier arms did not generate enough category-wide equity to justify pulling **Andy Pages** from the grass.\n\nRisk management is paramount today given the scarcity of our primary contributors. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** sidelined by scheduled off-days, and our depth bolstered only by the unfortunate reality of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** sitting on the IL, we are limited in our ability to pivot if these matchups turn sour. We are essentially riding our core through the gauntlet of Yamamoto and Sale, prioritizing the high-upside contact profile of **Jackson Merrill** to carry the weight while we wait for more favorable pitching conditions to re-engage the rest of the bench.",
